{"timestamp": "2026-05-28T10:28:27Z", "event": "afterAgentResponse", "role": "assistant", "text": "You’d mainly be changing the **election + prosperity model shape**, because right now each `VoterBlock` has a single `demographic` that controls **both** population identity and voting/economic behavior.\n\n## Primary files to change\n\n- `source/scenes/election_runtime.scene.dry`  \n  This is the core. You’d need to split block identity into something like:\n  - **population stratum** (for totals: first/second/third wave),\n  - **behavior stratum** (for voting + affluence/prosperity behavior, e.g. coop).  \n  Concretely, these parts are impacted:\n  - `VoterBlock` model (`demographic` usage everywhere)\n  - `buildVoterBlocks()` (currently 1 block per district×stratum)\n  - vote tabulation paths (`blockCompetitiveScores`, `claimedFraction`, `igContributionsForBlock`, `allocateCompetitiveVotes`, `tabulateBlock*`)\n  - poll exports and per-stratum rollups in `writePollDisplaysToQ()` (currently grouped by `block.demographic.id`)\n  - prosperity exports `qified_block_prosperity()` / `syncStratumProsperityAverages()` (currently averaged by demographic id)\n  - data definitions:\n    - `DISTRICT_POPULATIONS`\n    - `IG_MEMBERSHIP_BY_STRATUM`\n    - demographic config in `buildDemographics()`\n\n- `source/scenes/economic_assets_runtime.scene.dry`  \n  Affluence/housing behavior is keyed off `block.demographic.id` and `owner='coop'` etc. Dual allegiance means deciding whether housing/prosperity logic follows origin-wave or coop behavior and then updating:\n  - housing ledgers (`buildBlockHousingLedger`, `summarizeStratumDistrictBuckets`, borrow/lend logic)\n  - block-level stratum ownership checks in `economicHomeServesStratum` and downstream counters\n  - stratum/district population aggregation (`buildStratumDistrictPopulations`)\n  - prosperity application where ownerType `stratum` targets matching blocks\n\n- `source/scenes/cards/organizing/organize_phase_tick.scene.dry`  \n  Monthly prosperity transfer mesh and stratum bumps are stratum-keyed. Functions that use `block.demographic.id` would need to use your new behavior/origin axis consistently:\n  - `applyStratumProsperityBumps`\n  - district mesh and IG spill functions\n  - `ProsperityConnectionModifier.blocksMatching` logic for `scope === 'stratum'`\n\n## Secondary/UI files likely needing updates\n\n- `source/scenes/status.scene.dry`  \n  If you keep displaying “poll by stratum” and “prosperity by stratum,” you’ll need to define whether these rows are by origin-wave or by behavior-stratum and potentially add both views.\n\n- `source/scenes/library.scene.dry`  \n  Lore text probably needs updating to explain dual allegiance mechanics to players.\n\n## Dev mirror / simulation sync (optional but recommended)\n\n- `source/lib/election-world-data.js`\n- `source/lib/election-v2.js`  \n  These are dev/CLI mirrors; gameplay uses the `.scene.dry` runtime. But if you want `simulate-election:v2` parity (especially without/around `--from-scene` workflows), mirror the model changes here too.\n\n---\n\nBig picture: this is mostly a **data model refactor** in `election_runtime.scene.dry` from one-axis stratum identity to two-axis identity. Once that’s in place, most other edits are making every aggregation explicit about which axis it means (population totals vs voting/affluence behavior)."}
{"timestamp": "2026-05-28T10:38:39Z", "event": "beforeSubmitPrompt", "role": "user", "text": "an alternative way to approach this would be to make the coops into an interest group and allow interest groups in general to take populations from other demographics.\n\nFor this model I'd probably want to make shareholders a demographic and turn the \"rich\" demographic into an interest group (local capitalists) which would draw members from the 1st/2nd/3rd waves and deepers.  The guilds and gang interest groups would also draw from these groups (and the alien/otherworlders groups.)  Meanwhile the corporate interest groups would have memberships of the drones and shareholders.  Under this model it might make sense to make it so non-housing assets are explicitly owned by interest groups.", "meta": {"attachments": [{"type": "rule", "file_path": "source-directory.mdc"}, {"type": "rule", "file_path": "game-source-only.mdc"}, {"type": "rule", "file_path": "dendry.mdc"}]}}
{"timestamp": "2026-05-28T10:39:05Z", "event": "afterAgentResponse", "role": "assistant", "text": "That’s a strong direction, and it fits your current engine better than dual-identity voter blocks.\n\n## Why this model is cleaner\n\n- Your election model already supports IGs drawing fractional membership from multiple strata via `IG_MEMBERSHIP_BY_STRATUM`, then allocating ballots by party mix.\n- Keeping demographics as **population containers** and moving political/economic identity into **IG memberships** avoids rewriting every block-level election/prosperity function.\n- Turning coops + local capitalists into IGs gives you the “cross-cutting allegiance” behavior with much less structural risk.\n\n## What to change for this model\n\n- `source/scenes/election_runtime.scene.dry`\n  - Add new demographic: `shareholder` (in `STRATUM_IDS`, display map, populations, demographic config, UI export loops).\n  - Keep/remove `rich` as demographic based on your intended semantics (if “rich” becomes only local-capitalist IG, replace with shareholder + maybe managerial strata).\n  - Add new IGs in `buildInterestGroups()`:\n    - `Coops` (or similar)\n    - `LocalCapitalists` (replacement for rich political bloc)\n  - Rework `IG_MEMBERSHIP_BY_STRATUM` so:\n    - guilds/syndicates/coops/local capitalists draw from 1st/2nd/3rd/deeper (+alien where desired),\n    - corporate IGs draw primarily from `drone` + `shareholder`.\n  - Revisit `igClaimCap` values in `buildDemographics()` since much more competition for the same strata will otherwise clip hard at cap.\n\n- `source/scenes/economic_assets_runtime.scene.dry`\n  - This is the big economic semantics shift:\n    - today `ownerType: 'stratum'` drives non-home asset prosperity into that stratum’s blocks.\n    - if non-housing assets become IG-owned, route prosperity through `ownerType: 'ig'` and then spill to blocks via your prosperity link system.\n  - Likely reduce/phase out stratum-owned assets except housing stock.\n  - Update reporting labels/grouping so assets read as IG portfolios rather than demographic portfolios.\n\n- `source/scenes/cards/organizing/organize_phase_tick.scene.dry`\n  - Expand/tune IG prosperity spill (`PROSPERITY_IG_HOME_DISTRICT_LINKS`, effective pop constants) so IG-owned assets materially affect relevant populations.\n  - Add new IG prosperity tracks for new IGs (if you want market/index-style displays or economic weight).\n\n- `source/scenes/electorate_runtime.scene.dry`\n  - Most modifiers currently target strata/district/global.\n  - Decide whether some card/event effects should target IGs directly (you may want an `ig` scope in `ElectorateModifier` eventually, but not required immediately).\n\n- `source/scenes/status.scene.dry`\n  - Add display lines for shareholder polls/prosperity if shareholder is a full stratum.\n  - Consider adding an IG influence/ballot contribution section so players can see the new political structure.\n\n## Key design choices to lock first\n\n- Does `rich` disappear as a demographic entirely, or remain as a population class alongside a new local-capitalist IG?\n- Are IG memberships mutually exclusive or overlapping?\n  - Current engine assumes overlapping shares and normalizes under claim caps; that works, but behavior changes a lot as memberships increase.\n- Do you want IG membership to influence:\n  - only voting (current behavior),\n  - or also prosperity/housing access (would require explicit new rules).\n\nIf you want, I can draft a concrete migration spec next (exact new strata/IG tables and initial membership numbers) so you can implement this in one pass without breaking election balance."}
{"timestamp": "2026-05-28T10:42:37Z", "event": "beforeSubmitPrompt", "role": "user", "text": "oh another complication to this is that the drones technically would be members of the various waves.  But the drones are much more seperated in voting behavior and affluence then the coops are.  So maybe it would need to be that any member of any of the corporate interest groups gets converted into drones.  And if they leave the corporate interest group (i.e. get fired) they convert back.", "meta": {"attachments": [{"type": "rule", "file_path": "source-directory.mdc"}, {"type": "rule", "file_path": "game-source-only.mdc"}, {"type": "rule", "file_path": "dendry.mdc"}]}}
{"timestamp": "2026-05-28T10:42:51Z", "event": "afterAgentResponse", "role": "assistant", "text": "Yes — that’s a good way to model drones as a **derived labor status** instead of a fixed birth demographic.\n\n## Recommended rule\n\n- Treat `drone` as a **state generated by corporate IG membership**, not a base population bucket.\n- Base strata remain 1st/2nd/3rd/deeper/alien/shareholder/etc.\n- Each tick:\n  - if a person is in corporate IG membership -> they are counted as drone for voting + affluence\n  - if they exit corporate IG membership -> they revert to their origin stratum behavior\n\nThis gives you exactly the “fired -> back to wave identity” behavior.\n\n## Minimal-engine way to implement in your current architecture\n\nIn `election_runtime.scene.dry`, add a transformation layer before tabulation:\n\n- Keep `DISTRICT_POPULATIONS` as origin populations (no permanent drone bucket, or keep drone small/systemic if needed).\n- Compute a **derived effective block split**:\n  - `effectiveDronePop = sum(corporate IG claims on eligible origin strata)` (capped)\n  - `effectiveOriginPop = originPop - portion converted to drone`\n- Run voting with:\n  - converted portion using drone vote rules (`corp_or_abstain`, drone competitive scores/steepness)\n  - remaining portion using origin stratum behavior\n\nYou can do this either by:\n1) creating temporary “shadow blocks” for tabulation (cleanest), or  \n2) adjusting `tabulateBlockWithAbstention` math inline (faster, messier).\n\n## Important policy decisions\n\n- **Eligibility:** which strata can be drone-converted (likely 1st/2nd/3rd/deeper, maybe alien, maybe not shareholder).\n- **Priority when multiple corporate IGs overlap:** proportional split vs priority order.\n- **Persistence:** immediate month-to-month recalculation (simple) vs employment inertia (more realistic).\n- **Prosperity ownership:** converted workers use drone affluence dynamics while employed; on exit they inherit origin-stratum dynamics again.\n\n## Files this specifically touches\n\n- `source/scenes/election_runtime.scene.dry` (core derived-conversion logic, tabulation, poll outputs)\n- `source/scenes/economic_assets_runtime.scene.dry` (housing/prosperity handling for converted drone population)\n- `source/scenes/cards/organizing/organize_phase_tick.scene.dry` (prosperity links and bump behavior for derived drone mass)\n- optionally `source/scenes/status.scene.dry` (show “origin population” vs “currently drone-employed”)\n\nIf you want, I can sketch the exact data model and function signatures for the shadow-block approach next — that’s probably the safest implementation path."}
