{"timestamp": "2026-05-28T11:46:39Z", "event": "afterAgentResponse", "role": "assistant", "text": "Yes — this is a solid outline, but I do see some omissions you’ll probably want to pin down.\n\n- **Unaligned population bucket missing:** if `non_ig_population` is used for stratum voting/affluence, define who is in *no IG* at a given time and ensure they still vote (or intentionally abstain).\n- **IG overlap rule missing:** can one person belong to multiple IGs (guild + coop, syndicate + owners)? If not, you need precedence/exclusivity rules.\n- **Entry/exit mechanics missing:** you mention shrinking IGs, but not how movement is computed each tick (rates, triggers, hysteresis, cooldown).\n- **Drone conversion specifics missing:** you noted this earlier, but here it doesn’t state whether *all* corporate IG members become drone, and exactly what they revert to when they leave.\n- **Shareholder locality edge case:** if many shareholders are off-world, decide whether they count in district population, only exec/guild voting, or as a separate non-resident electorate.\n- **District allocation for IG members:** IGs draw from strata, but votes are tabulated by district blocks; you need a district assignment rule for converted IG members.\n- **Affluence/prosperity routing missing:** “independent affluence” is stated, but not whether IG prosperity is per-IG only, then spilled to members, or whether members retain any stratum prosperity effects.\n- **Housing/asset ownership policy incomplete:** you suggest non-housing assets should be IG-owned; define whether stratum-owned non-home assets are eliminated or grandfathered.\n- **Existing actors not mapped:** current model has `Executive` and `Gold`; your list has `Pink` replacing part of Gold, but doesn’t define where remaining Gold/Executive power lands.\n- **Display/reporting omissions:** if drones/syndicates are bundled in UI, decide whether simulation logic is also bundled or only display-level bundling.\n\nAlso minor text fix