{"timestamp": "2026-05-28T13:50:24Z", "event": "afterAgentResponse", "role": "assistant", "text": "Yes. In Cursor (VS Code-based), you can disable suggestions specifically for plain text (`.txt`) files.\n\nAdd this to your `settings.json`:\n\n```json\n\"[plaintext]\": {\n  \"editor.quickSuggestions\": false,\n  \"editor.suggestOnTriggerCharacters\": false,\n  \"editor.wordBasedSuggestions\": \"off\"\n}\n```\n\nIf you still see popups, also disable inline completions for plaintext:\n\n```json\n\"[plaintext]\": {\n  \"editor.inlineSuggest.enabled\": false\n}\n```\n\nQuick way: open Command Palette -> `Preferences: Open Settings (JSON)` -> paste those blocks."}
