{"timestamp": "2026-05-28T13:57:12Z", "event": "afterAgentResponse", "role": "assistant", "text": "If you mean **Preferences/Settings are opening as read-only**, usually it’s one of these:\n\n- You opened **Default Settings** (`defaultSettings.json`) — that file is always read-only.\n- You’re in a **restricted folder/workspace** with limited permissions.\n- You opened settings from an extension/package file instead of your user/workspace settings.\n\nUse this instead:\n\n- Command Palette -> `Preferences: Open User Settings (JSON)`  \n  (this is editable)\n- Or `Preferences: Open Workspace Settings (JSON)`  \n  (editable for current project)\n\nIf it still says read-only, check file permissions on your settings file (`~/.config/Cursor/User/settings.json` on Linux) and make sure your user owns it.\n\nIf you want, I can walk you through fixing permissions step-by-step."}
