{"timestamp": "2026-05-28T18:36:15Z", "event": "afterAgentThought", "role": "assistant_thought", "text": "So the answer is clear: There is no function that automatically copies scene JS into `source/lib/*.js` test files.\n\nThe process involves scripts/extract-scene-js.js extracting JavaScript code from .scene.dry files between MIKASA_*_BEGIN and END markers, then either printing to stdout or evaluating it in Node.js. Test scripts like simulate-election.js and simulate-prosperity-months.js require this module and execute the scene code in memory using the --from-scene flag.", "meta": {"duration_ms": 2106}}
{"timestamp": "2026-05-28T18:36:22Z", "event": "afterAgentResponse", "role": "assistant", "text": "There isn’t a script that **writes** scene JavaScript into `source/lib/*.js` test mirrors. Extraction is **read + eval in Node**, not copy-to-file.\n\nThe tool is **`scripts/extract-scene-js.js`**.\n\nMain pieces:\n\n| Function | What it does |\n|----------|----------------|\n| `extractRuntimeBlock(text, blockName)` | Pulls JS between `// MIKASA_<BLOCK>_BEGIN` and `// MIKASA_<BLOCK>_END` |\n| `extractRuntimeBlockFromFile(scenePath, blockName)` | Reads a `.scene.dry` and calls the above |\n| `loadRuntimeBlock(blockName, options)` | Extracts + `eval()` into `global.Q` |\n| `loadGameRuntimes(options)` | Loads election + electorate (and optional blocks) in order |\n| `extractOnArrivalJs(scenePath)` | Legacy: grabs the whole `on-arrival: {! … !}` block |\n| `loadSceneOnArrival(scenePath, options)` | Evals that on-arrival block |\n\nScene map is in `RUNTIME_SCENES` (e.g. `ELECTION_RUNTIME` → `election_runtime.scene.dry`).\n\n**Who uses it for “tests”:**\n\n- `scripts/simulate-election.js` — with `--from-scene`, calls `loadGameRuntimes()` from `extract-scene-js.js` instead of `source/lib/election-v2.js`\n- `scripts/simulate-prosperity-months.js` — `require('./extract-scene-js.js')` and loads multiple runtime scenes\n\nCLI examples:\n\n```bash\nnode scripts/extract-scene-js.js --list\nnode scripts/extract-scene-js.js ELECTION_RUNTIME   # prints extracted JS to stdout\nnode scripts/simulate-election.js --v2 --from-scene\n```\n\n**Opposite direction (lib → scene, not scene → lib):**  \n`scripts/sync-economic-name-catalog-to-scene.js` copies from `source/lib/economic-asset-name-catalog.js` **into** `economic_assets_runtime.scene.dry`.\n\n**`source/lib/election-v2.js` etc.** are hand-maintained dev mirrors; the repo expects you to edit `.scene.dry` first and mirror manually (or always use `--from-scene` for sims).\n\nIf you meant “where does Dendry compile scenes into playable JS,” that’s **`npm run make-html`** (dendrynexus → `out/html/core.js`), not `extract-scene-js.js`."}
